<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="17efc19">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product contains the detailed design that lays out how the selected data will be represented in any given
    report.  Depending on the environment the reports are to be created in the specifications may range from a
    simple layout and mapping to data sources to a set of detailed specifications including scripts and
    detailed program logic along with standard classes or modules to be included.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="bb08da70"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="8dad713c">&lt;p&gt;
    Even in the case of packages that are supplied with existing reports it will often be necessary to customize them to
    some extent.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="68510cb8"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="d10575b0">To clearly defined what is expected on any reports along with the expected data sources and frequency of execution in
order to make sure what is produced meets stakeholder expectations.  The specifications form the basis for the testing
of the generated reports.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="1e680c04">If this work product is not produced it is likely that some needed reports may not get produced or that several different
versions of the same report may be created.  Additionally, if the reports are not fully specified, not all of the
required data may be available.</attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="60575f3a">This work product is may not needed for ad hoc reports.</attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="856dd78d">&lt;p&gt;
    Report Specifications are documents containing the following attributes for each report to be created:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Report Name
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Intended Audience
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Report Definition 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Expected Parameters
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Business Rules
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Formatting and layout
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Data Sources 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Attribute mapping
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Currency
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Execution Considerations 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Frequency of report generations
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Delivery mechanism / access to reports, including how the reports are invoked and distributed
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Error handling
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
